From: hemgo-lexsi <hem.gosalia@lexsi.ai>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:36:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] local checkpoints: config and model class from
 config.json, not the path

convert_hf_model_config chose the architecture, and for 29 branches the
whole config, from substrings of the model name. A local checkpoint's
directory name is arbitrary: a fine-tuned "meta-llama-Llama-3.2-1B_sft"
folder loaded with base Llama-3.2-1B's hard-coded config and never read
its own config.json, and other Llama-named folders crashed on
hf_config=None. For a local directory with a config.json, the chain now
sees an empty name, so the architecture comes from config.json and only
architecture-keyed branches match (Llama: the generic LlamaForCausalLM
branch). get_pretrained_state_dict picks a local checkpoint's model class
from its architecture instead of "bert" / "t5" / "hubert" / "wav2vec2" in
the path. Hub names are unchanged.
---
 transformer_lens/loading_from_pretrained.py | 34 ++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/transformer_lens/loading_from_pretrained.py b/transformer_lens/loading_from_pretrained.py
index 1f80721..bd33dd8 100644
